<title>JAPAN: RTRS-Landesbank launches 3.05 pct reverse yen/A$ samurai.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Landesbank launches 3.05 pct reverse yen/A$ samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian reverse dual-currency samurai bond issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Securities on Tuesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Landesbank Rheinland-Pfalz AG</p>
<p> AMT		 15 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.05 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  27 March 2007</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  27 March 1997</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	March 19</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA+, Moody's Aa1, JCR AAA</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan</p>
<p>NOTES: The coupon will be paid in Australian dollars, while redemption will be in yen. The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,211.04 per 500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
